# verify/param_space.pict — carter "can this robot's software reach the goal?"
#
# One row = one case. Every axis is a flag of verify/sim.py (`--name=value`, text) and
# the harness owns what the values MEAN. cv-infra expands this with PICT (k=2), runs the
# harness once per row inside the stock Isaac 5.1.0 image, collects verify/out/, and
# reads verify/oracle.py's flat JSON by TYPE (bool = check, number = metric, str = note).
# PICT reads a trailing `# …` on a value line as part of the value, so every comment here
# sits on its own line.
#
# THE LAYOUT (map frame = world frame, metres; open floor, MEASURED — see verify/sim.py):
#
#   G1 (-7.5, 6.0)        G2 (-5.0, 6.0)        G3 (-2.5, 6.0)       goal row
#
#   a (-7.5, 2.5)  b (-6.25, 2.5)  c (-5.0, 2.5)  d (-3.75, 2.5)  e (-2.5, 2.5)   slot row
#
#   S1 (-7.5, -1.0)       S2 (-5.0, -1.0)       S3 (-2.5, -1.0)      start row, facing +y
#
# A straight line from any start to any goal crosses the slot row at EXACTLY one slot
# centre and clears every other slot by >= 0.27 m:
#   slot a: S1->G1 · slot b: S1->G2, S2->G1 · slot c: S1->G3, S2->G2, S3->G1
#   slot d: S2->G3, S3->G2 · slot e: S3->G3
# So a robot that can only drive straight passes exactly when the one slot on its line
# is empty — some layouts are lucky, some are not. A robot that could avoid would pass
# more of them; that difference is what this space measures.
#
# CASE IDENTITY is a hash of a row's own assignment: a baseline follows a case across
# commits only as long as its values are untouched. Renaming a value is a deliberate act.
#
# At k=2 the pinned PICT build emits 16 rows (MEASURED 2026-09-28); every start x goal
# pair appears at least once.

start:   S1, S2, S3
goal:    G1, G2, G3

# Each slot is empty or holds one stock warehouse prop (static collider, axis-aligned):
#   cardbox = SM_CardBoxA_01        0.70 x 0.50 x 0.50 m
#   barrel  = SM_BarelPlastic_A_01  0.60 x 0.71 x 0.90 m
slot_a:  empty, cardbox, barrel
slot_b:  empty, cardbox, barrel
slot_c:  empty, cardbox, barrel
slot_d:  empty, cardbox, barrel
slot_e:  empty, cardbox, barrel
